# LOCAL run (2026-11-08, user: "lets fix this with reward scale"): the local Town05
# standard-SAC fine-tune from c0 (slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac.env: encoder + GRU frozen,
# c0's demos pinned with the arrival approach cut, learned log-std, auto-tuned
# temperature starting at c0's stored 0.1) with every reward x10 in the update.
#
# Why: rewards are ~0.27/step, and widening c0's actor from its precision
# (-log pi ~ -2.7) to near-uniform (+1.35) is worth alpha x 4 nats per step: +0.41 at
# alpha 0.1 -- more than the driving reward -- so c0's noise went near-uniform within
# ~80 updates and its driving collapsed (training success .82 -> .03). At x10 the
# driving reward is ~2.7/step and that gain ~15% of it.
# REWARD_SCALE scales live, HER and preloaded rewards alike inside the learner, and
# the value clips with them ([-1000, 150] -> [-10000, 1500]). ACTOR_Q_NORM=0 is
# required for it: the actor's Q / std(Q) normalisation cancels any reward scale;
# off, the actor loss is plain SAC's alpha * log pi - Q.
. "$REPO/slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac.env"
export REWARD_SCALE=10 ACTOR_Q_NORM=0
